      "title": "Circular Rydberg atoms set new stability records",
      "summary": "Physicists at the University of Stuttgart created circular Rydberg atoms — a special high-angular-momentum atomic state — that stayed stable for a record 11 milliseconds, alongside record size and storage time. Longer-lived, larger circular Rydberg states make them more practical building blocks for quantum computers and simulators, since decoherence has long limited their use. The atoms remain a laboratory achievement, still far from being wired into a working large-scale quantum processor.",
      "source": "Phys.org",
      "published": "2026-09-16T19:20+00:00",
      "url": "https://phys.org/news/2026-09-circular-rydberg-atoms-staying-stable.html"
    },
